{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/39120","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:44.177280+00:00","comments":[],"issue":{"active_lock_reason":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"author_association":"NONE","body":"### Description\n\nAs I wrote tests for an overlap-save fft convolution, I realized that `jit` compiling the function resulted in flaky, sometimes very large, deviation from the correct result. \n\nBy doing some investigation, I think I figured out what could have been the cause: `jnp.pad` followed by nested `lax.scan`s that `dynamic_slice` overlapping blocks returns uninitialized memory (NaN, denormals, huge values) where the pad row should be exactly 0.0. Eager execution (`jax.disable_jit`) is always correct.\n\nBelow a small script that reproduce (in most runs) the bug.\n\n```python\n\nimport sys\n\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport numpy as np\n\nN, C = 60, 4  # input rows, columns\nBLOCK, STEP, NBLOCKS = 23, 19, 3  # overlapping blocks: rows [i*19, i*19 + 23)\nNPAD = 61  # (NBLOCKS - 1) * STEP + BLOCK; one zero row appended\nCHUNK = 2  # inner scan slices column pairs\n\n\n@jax.jit\ndef f(x):\n    x = jnp.pad(x, ((0, NPAD - N), (0, 0)))  # append one row of zeros\n\n    def outer(_, i):\n        blk = jax.lax.dynamic_slice(x, (i * STEP, 0), (BLOCK, C))\n\n        def inner(_, j):\n            return None, jax.lax.dynamic_slice(blk, (0, j * CHUNK), (BLOCK, CHUNK))\n\n        _, ys = jax.lax.scan(inner, None, jnp.arange(C // CHUNK))\n        return None, ys\n\n    _, out = jax.lax.scan(outer, None, jnp.arange(NBLOCKS))\n    return out\n\n\nx = jax.random.normal(jax.random.PRNGKey(0), (N, C))\nresult = np.asarray(f(x))\n\n# the last row of the last block is the appended zero row: it must be exactly 0\npad_row = result[-1, :, -1, :]\nif np.all(pad_row == 0.0):\n    print(\"ok: pad row is zero\")\n    sys.exit(0)\nprint(f\"BUG: pad row read as {pad_row.ravel()} (expected exact zeros)\")\nsys.exit(1)\n\n```\n\nAnd blow a few output I obtained, note the presence of NaNs but also of large values (1.2606397e+21).\n\n```\nObserved output (12 fresh processes):\n    BUG: pad row read as [1.4739792e-35 1.6815582e-44 2.7404502e-34 1.6815582e-44]\n    BUG: pad row read as [   nan    nan 1.e-45 1.e-45]\n    BUG: pad row read as [0.0000000e+00 0.0000000e+00 2.8069184e+12 9.8090893e-45]\n    BUG: pad row read as [nan nan nan nan]\n    BUG: pad row read as [3.e-45 0.e+00 0.e+00 0.e+00]\n    ok: pad row is zero\n    BUG: pad row read as [1.2606397e+21 1.5414283e-44 4.9011089e+22 1.5414283e-44]\n    BUG: pad row read as [nan nan nan nan]\n    BUG: pad row read as [-7.544458e-04  1.261169e-44  4.203895e-45  4.203895e-45]\n    BUG: pad row read as [7.631201e+24 1.401298e-44 1.301149e+23 1.401298e-44]\n    BUG: pad row read as [-2.5189768e-13  1.4012985e-44 -2.7766133e-14  1.4012985e-44]\n    BUG: pad row read as [   nan    nan 1.e-45 1.e-45]\n    === reproduced in 11/12 processes ===\n```\n\n### System info (python version, jaxlib version, accelerator, etc.)\n\n```\njax:    0.9.0\njaxlib: 0.9.0\nnumpy:  2.3.5\npython: 3.13.11 (main, Jan 28 2026, 21:41:04) [Clang 21.1.8 ]\ndevice info: cpu-1, 1 local devices\"\nprocess_count: 1\nplatform: uname_result(system='Darwin', node='PHH9L02RFN', release='25.5.0', version='Darwin Kernel Version 25.5.0: Mon Apr 27 20:39:09 PDT 2026; root:xnu-12377.121.6~2/RELEASE_ARM64_T6020', machine='arm64')\n```","closed_at":null,"closed_by":null,"comments":0,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/39120/comments","created_at":"2026-07-13T14:52:51Z","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/39120/events","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/39120","id":4874820949,"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"total_blocking":0},"issue_field_values":[],"labels":[{"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null,"color":"d73a4a","default":true,"description":"Something isn't working","id":1104782284,"name":"bug","node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwxMTA0NzgyMjg0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/labels/bug"}],"labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/39120/labels{/name}","locked":false,"milestone":null,"node_id":"I_kwDOCTkjjc8AAAABIo_dVQ","number":39120,"performed_via_github_app":null,"pinned_comment":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/39120/reactions"},"repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax","state":"open","state_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"completed":0,"percent_completed":0,"total":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/39120/timeline","title":"XLA:CPU float32 miscompilation: zero-padding read back as garbage under jit.","type":null,"updated_at":"2026-07-13T14:52:51Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/39120","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/28624715?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BalzaniEdoardo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BalzaniEdoardo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BalzaniEdoardo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BalzaniEdoardo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/BalzaniEdoardo","id":28624715,"login":"BalzaniEdoardo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjI0NzE1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BalzaniEdoardo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BalzaniEdoardo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BalzaniEdoardo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BalzaniEdoardo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BalzaniEdoardo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BalzaniEdoardo","user_view_type":"public"}},"pages":{"comments":[{"page":1,"records":0,"sha25